{"name":"Iroko","hex":"#433120","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"iroko","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Hardwood obtained from the species Milicia excelsa and, less frequently, Milicia regia, often sold as African teak.","Any member of species Milicia excelsa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iroko"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iroko","blocks":[{"text":"Iroko is a large hardwood tree from the west coast of tropical Africa that can live up to 500 years. This is the common name for the genus Milicia, in which there are two recognized species, which are closely related: Milicia excelsa and Milicia regia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Milicia_roadside_small.jpg/330px-Milicia_roadside_small.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iroko","wikidata":"Q2324635"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Iroko_tree.jpg/500px-Iroko_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Iroko_tree.jpg/1280px-Iroko_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Iroko_tree.jpg/500px-Iroko_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Iroko tree","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIroko_tree.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Iroko-piece.jpg/500px-Iroko-piece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Iroko-piece.jpg/500px-Iroko-piece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A specimen of Iroko wood","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIroko-piece.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}